      "writtenOn": "2026-02-18T18:35:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s do this cleanup to mask.h as a separate CL prior to this one.\n\nThere\u0027s some subtlety that is lost here in that the types of the subsequent Es will be deduced by the compiler and could be different than the first E. Which means we could mix and match constants, which is what this class is trying to make impossible.\n\nWe wrote this prior to C++20, so we couldn\u0027t write the following \n```\ntemplate \u003cstd::same_as\u003cE\u003e... Args\u003e\nconstexpr Mask(E first, Args... rest)\n    : val_((static_cast\u003cUnderlyingType\u003e(first) | ... | static_cast\u003cUnderlyingType\u003e(rest))) {}\n```\n\nwhich is what I think we want.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 28,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "feb35cc5b46c3d7de4b51ac595ecd0e66d465bc3",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
